{"title":"2020 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Calculus_Needed)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Calculus Needed)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b3616aa71bc319235620f9b6bc531ed259bea539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(2^t-3t)t}{4^t}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"39\" /> for real values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/e/a9ea17c74559a5d70a472182278c4b1c67b4c038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1d45dfaa825fdb9e413ed8a714b8cf141d2b6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{16} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{15} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{12} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{10} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"404\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We proceed by using AM-GM. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d10d15f47aae497eaf0c90b7fa725674e47f70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(2^t-3t) + 3t}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"40\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/b/cbba187e93d2b0619abf3862fffc9f9a08b08c51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge \\sqrt{(2^t-3t)(3t)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"134\" height=\"32\" />. Thus, squaring gives us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1f0af16b5d52da563a6cc6e464bf01a5d1ed3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{t-1} \\ge (2^t-3t)(3t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"19\" />. Remembering what we want to find, we divide both sides of the inequality by the positive amount of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c4ed93e90bc57ec56b23125883d27c6f0ee772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3\\cdot4^t}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"39\" height=\"37\" />. We get the maximal values as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b3609b655e07048042e2e40e51d522f1be370c38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(C)   \\frac{1}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"64\" height=\"49\" />, and we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c5dd4b35abd0d37afa6623385a754ec506b0074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = t2^{-t}$\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" />. Then the expression in the problem can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/8/0f85ef357006641b26feaafa9a58fb205490f6a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R = - 3t^24^{-t} + t2^{-t}= - 3u^2 + u = - 3 (u - 1/6)^2 + \\frac{1}{12} \\le \\frac{1}{12} .\\]\" width=\"475\" height=\"37\" /> It is easy to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/149a322d7a6312781d472cb0a44ab9c4ba38a1ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u =\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> is attained for some value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/8/288e2a39b58d673182c57dc6214b702a448341ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 0$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c30bbb3a66ef235e5183332e4bdd8bc0972d31d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />, thus the maximal value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d1f1b44225831ab21c4e971ee2b4da9be88235c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Calculus_Needed.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Calculus_Needed)\">Solution 3 (Calculus Needed)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Calculus Needed)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/f/04f9e77081ccdf84c566d3922fd88b1410fa61fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t) = \\frac{(2^t-3t)t}{4^t} = \\frac{t\\cdot 2^t-3t^2}{4^t}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"239\" height=\"39\" />. We can use the first derivative test. Use quotient rule to get the following:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bf190efc71fa42949deb99575601335f9ddb7f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(2^t + t\\cdot \\ln{2} \\cdot 2^t - 6t)4^t - (t\\cdot 2^t - 3t^2)4^t \\cdot 2\\ln{2}}{(4^t)^2} = 0 \\implies 2^t + t\\cdot \\ln{2} \\cdot 2^t - 6t = (t\\cdot 2^t - 3t^2) 2\\ln{2}\\]\" width=\"706\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a4e4a0b40f6567e4ac1e5b656a24699d8e02095.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 2^t + t\\cdot \\ln{2}\\cdot 2^t - 6t = 2t\\ln{2} \\cdot 2^t - 6t^2 \\ln{2}\\]\" width=\"361\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/72556dcef8ef45b7978dd38c5d500c1731874a79.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 2^t(1-t\\cdot \\ln{2}) = 6t(1 - t\\cdot \\ln{2}) \\implies 2^t = 6t\\]\" width=\"381\" height=\"19\" />Therefore, we plug this back into the original equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf0ff6ceb60fd04617d9a4ba20ea02f33b48448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\frac{1}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"62\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~awesome1st\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22dc2f9780cac7b12ccd85c28d6a9c439749b53c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^t = x (\\log_2{x} = t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"19\" /> so that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64446edcf5c1063abb3117f3b5e766925e52351.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(2^t-3t)t}{4^t} = \\frac{x\\log_2{x}-3(\\log_2{x})^2}{x^2}\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Notice that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/a/c1ab8cc031d3df6a1298d63f66b93bd111812460.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x\\log_2{x}-3(\\log_2{x})^2}{x^2} = \\frac{\\log_2{x}}{x}-3\\Big(\\frac{\\log_2{x}}{x}\\Big)^2.\\]\" width=\"341\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>When seen as a function, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f1dfbe656e4e3a1e15e61299174d2b78267c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_2{x}}{x}-3\\Big(\\frac{\\log_2{x}}{x}\\Big)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"155\" height=\"37\" /> is a synthesis function that has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d9507fd2060d0208dc0fb05eac2e44efcbf60d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_2{x}}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> as its inner function.\n</p><p>If we substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d689b179f13138f61a267271ff10ad493755fa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_2{x}}{x} = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"81\" height=\"37\" />, the given function becomes a quadratic function that has a maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e10f7b229549d9afbdef6ae2862bc89bacfe16cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d6c744e10ea6d68ea6c71d9cd143f47349cb995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNow we need to check if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d9507fd2060d0208dc0fb05eac2e44efcbf60d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_2{x}}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> can have the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> in the range of real numbers.\n</p><p>In the range of (positive) real numbers, function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d9507fd2060d0208dc0fb05eac2e44efcbf60d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_2{x}}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> is a continuous function whose value gets infinitely smaller as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gets closer to 0 (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/7/d97c59f0c4d3f6697608cd2ab561d2292ce89bde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$log_2{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> also diverges toward negative infinity in the same condition). When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/8/fa8821a7adf412eb355cc6623094571a55828be7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_2{x}}{x} = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"84\" height=\"37\" />, which is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, we can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d9507fd2060d0208dc0fb05eac2e44efcbf60d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_2{x}}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> equals to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is somewhere between 1 and 2 (at least), which means that the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b3616aa71bc319235620f9b6bc531ed259bea539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(2^t-3t)t}{4^t}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"39\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f632f488ac109abafea8963fb6375b4bcd52f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"68\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the maximum value of the function be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f0e8b66179046481dc13c67700d909e857fd08b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(2^t-3t)t}{4^t} = m \\implies m2^{2t} - t2^t + 3t^2 = 0.\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"39\" />\nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fa027eb47c930ab21e21ed85553495484cd4a04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{t}$\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" />, we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34ccee6da13fb22af06f96362257c58d18e7820d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{t} = \\frac{t}{2m} \\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{t^2 - 12mt^2}}{2m} = \\frac{t}{2m} \\pm \\frac{t\\sqrt{1 - 12m}}{2m}.\\]\" width=\"363\" height=\"40\" /> We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db4cb383b59133bedef904228ee17a745f875eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - 12m \\geq 0 \\implies m \\leq \\frac{1}{12}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"214\" height=\"37\" /> Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f632f488ac109abafea8963fb6375b4bcd52f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"68\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2113ce1ae9bd08cd6fe9662d55cd05c923c3fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=2^t.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> Then, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/7896634b3c100ca23525dd5a04c38ff0dcf4fdf0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\left(2^t-3t\\right)t}{4^t}=\\frac{\\left(z-3t\\right)t}{z^2} = \\frac{-3t^2+zt}{z^2}.\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Upon inspection, the numerator of this expression grows at a relatively faster rate than the denominator, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>As the numerator is a quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> with a negative leading coefficient, its maximum value occurs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/e/c5eb2aade11780f86dd97fe9d0519a3b5befd720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\frac{-z}{2\\cdot -3}=\\frac{z}{6},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"125\" height=\"39\" /> or when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/d/03d5f41c44267caf23c2505d0b951c07a247c233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6t=2^t.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> Therefore, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09ddaa029b905f6471a5f1192f884e5f8bc89902.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\left(2^t-3t\\right)t}{4^t}=\\frac{\\left(6t-3t\\right)t}{(6t)^2}=\\frac{3t^2}{36t^2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{12}}.\\]\" width=\"340\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><br />\n-Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(fast)\">Solution 7 (fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b63551139a7c27500d787dd2b39d333c4186fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{(2^t-3t)t}{4^t}=\\dfrac{t\\cdot 2^t}{4^t}-\\dfrac{3t^2}{4^t}=\\dfrac{t}{2^t}-3\\left(\\dfrac{t}{2^t}\\right)^2.\\]\" width=\"324\" height=\"46\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/8/e983dbdf3df18b279d5a1ac4268408c4646473bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{t}{2^t}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" /> Then, the expression becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bed4cb1a153b3594b41f38eeb0fdabd3f7196e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-3x^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> which is minimized at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a40c9c10b928a26c578d04585c8c5596327a8b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />, giving a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35af86a0576f38ba18ebccc6c4612726c647c595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{12}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"75\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bba79c79e0a7ed73e4a1195ee237aaad4aa33415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{t}{2^t}=\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" /> is possible as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/806d7ee22305b3c7a64698c11333f849abe13f1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{t}{2^t}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"21\" height=\"38\" /> is continuous and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbce4b6d25d055aebd2e533a84fd45a94b7ef9de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{0}{2^0}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55d7863faf5f5b8c1b994d5cac8232abc5214da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{2^2}=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" /> so by the Intermediate Value Theorem (or just by intuition), there must be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a00bcfe66c297188ccd8da8800842124db25e849.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{t}{2^t}=\\frac{1}{6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~BS2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution1\">Video Solution1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/c2_b18Lv7c4\">https://youtu.be/c2_b18Lv7c4</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Problem starts at 2:10 in this video: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5HRSzpdJaX0&amp;t=130s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5HRSzpdJaX0&amp;t=130s</a>\n</p><p>-MistyMathMusic\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B\" title=\"2020 AMC 12B\">2020 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a><